  "section": "14",
  "quote": "A provision in a tenancy agreement prohibiting the presence of animals in or about the residential complex is void.",
  "reason": "Section 14 of the Residential Tenancies Act, 2006 renders any lease clause prohibiting animals in a rental unit void. Even though allergies may be grounds for the Landlord and Tenant Board to later order an eviction, a blanket prohibition in the tenancy agreement itself remains void."
}

